WEBVTT

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.260
Something is... broken?

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:05.430
Quantum computers... Infinite evolution...
The I.A.L. corporation...

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:09.140
Naga... It all began with this, huh?

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.070
<i>Kyo! Something important's happened!</i>

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.080
Don't scare me like that!

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.950
Besides, me studying history right
now is kind of important, too.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.910
<i>Forget that! This is about Ryoko!</i>

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.990
Hey! Is it true?!

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:30.000
Is it true that Kaminagi's still alive?!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.260
Where?! Where is she?!

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.660
Inside of the Altair.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.330
In the Zega?!

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.270
It still isn't definite.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:42.970
There just may be a chance that
we can restore her, though.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.600
We're salvaging her data.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.180
Like we once did for you, Kyo.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.990
Due to the transmission
interference during your last battle,

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:58.420
it was assumed that Ryoko Kaminagi's
data had been completely lost.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.720
<i>Entangle, time out.</i>

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:05.160
However, while the data comprising
her didn't transfer to the Oceanus,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.120
it remained within the Altair's
meta-body data buffer.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.970
If enough of her memory and
personality data are left,

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.570
we can regenerate her body
using her genetic data...

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.910
and restore Ryoko as she used to be.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:23.210
Right now, we're investigating
just how damaged her data is.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.350
This is?

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.650
Ms. Mizusawa!
Please listen to what I have to say!

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.550
No. Maybe if I play it straight,
but with a lighter touch...

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.220
Ms. Mizusawa, the fact is,
the way I feel about you is...

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.190
No, that's not right.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.690
Ms. Mizusawa...

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.230
Multidimensional holographic
data analysis, complete.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.450
I believe there is a high probability that
Ryoko Kaminagi's data can be salvaged.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:29.610
Really?!

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.840
That's wonderful!

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.410
This should cheer things up
here on the bridge again!

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.060
Yeah!

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.390
But I wonder if she'll be any use to
us in battle once she's recovered.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.550
All right. Suspend salvage
operations for now.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.730
Knowing she can be
salvaged is enough.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.970
Reroute the system load
to the development section.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.530
Give top priority to the development
of the Sparrow and the Holo-Bolt.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.300
Aye, sir!

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.210
You look like you want to say something.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.150
No, sir. It's nothing.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.340
Feel free.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.790
Your father was the chairman
of the Mao Enterprise Group,

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.720
the main sponsor of I.A.L. Corp.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.060
It was through your peoples' efforts
that humanity could escape...

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.660
into the quantum servers
when it faced extinction.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:23.030
Which is another way of
saying that we were the ones...

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:25.090
who led mankind to its destruction.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.510
Aside from that, isn't it you who
has something to say to me?

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.780
Just that I see you act
in a very precise manner.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.540
And that sometimes you might
even go right over my head.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.220
You mean how I went
to Maihama on my own?

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.120
Or that I talked to Kyo?

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.420
Both, actually.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.590
In both cases, the passage
of time forced the decision.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:49.030
What I wanted or didn't
want had nothing to do with it.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.620
Of course. It's no problem.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.120
For now, at least.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:06.810
Where is this place?

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.980
It's so cute!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.590
Hey. Did you know?

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:22.560
This species of dolphin attacks people.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:23.720
You big liar!

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:26.630
Huh?

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.470
What?

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.230
Haven't we done this before?

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:32.070
Yeah, your gags are just
as lame as they always are.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:37.110
No, not that.
Haven't we come here before?

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.010
No, we couldn't have.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.040
This is my first time here, too.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.220
Is this what they call déjà vu?

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:47.390
No! Maybe it's precognition!

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:51.190
Hey, maybe I'll be able to
predict the future from now on...

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:57.920
Oh, yeah.
We were gonna fall in here, like this.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.830
If you knew, why didn't you
keep us from falling in?!

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.030
Why isn't anyone else showing up?!

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.360
Aren't we trying to get to the nationals?!

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.100
You want some, Hayase?

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:01.120
Ms. Mizusawa. Is something wrong?

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:02.980
Mr. Kurashige...

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:07.470
Um, when I saw you rush off
before with that look on your face,

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.700
I tried to come after you.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:13.070
But, for some reason,
I can't seem to leave the school.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.340
Any idea what's going on?

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.140
Mr. Kurashige!

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.040
Mizusawa...

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.680
I don't understand!
I just don't understand!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.100
Oh!

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.370
Commander Shima is so cruel!

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.330
In what way?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.170
<i>Every</i> way!

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:44.670
I'd tend to agree.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.700
Hell yeah!

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:50.480
We're so close to saving Ryoko,
and he just!

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:53.710
No, on that point, he's totally correct.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:58.950
Right now, gaining a way to
counter the Anti-Zega has priority.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.590
No way!

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:04.520
I think it's better for Kyo now, too.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.450
He'll have enough to deal with soon...

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:11.890
He'll need time to take in a lot of things.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:20.000
Vehicle silhouette, bearing 2 o'clock!
Quantum weapons, detected!

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.310
This pattern is!

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:23.210
It's him!

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.710
Anti-Zega Coatlicue seems to
have locked on to the Garuda!

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:32.250
The Garuda is taking evasive action.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:32.920
Where's Chris?

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.080
Boarded and standing by! He's awaiting launch!

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.460
Scramble! Have him support the Garuda!

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.460
Hraesvelg, prepare for transmission!

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:41.320
Yehl.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.730
<i>Coatlicue will reach Garuda in 90 seconds!</i>

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:49.270
At last, she shows her face. You ready?

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.600
Yeah, I figured I'd tag along with you.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:56.270
Don't be modest. You're the Wizard who
protected that kid's backside. I trust you.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.940
Thanks. You know how
to make a girl feel welcome.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.250
<i>Countdown, initiated. Transmission</i>
<i>scatter rate, confirmed.</i>

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.080
<i>E.X. condition, green!</i>

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.120
<i>Bednorz parameter, stable.</i>

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.140
<i>Bednorz curve, steady!</i>

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:14.550
<i>Materialization probability flux 99.992 C.C.A.T.</i>

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:16.530
<i>Recovery coordinates, set and locked!</i>

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:18.390
<i>Hraesvelg, transmit!</i>

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.060
Entangle!

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.440
<i>She's coming back.</i>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.410
<i>Kaminagi's coming back!</i>

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.210
Kyo.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.180
Kyo...

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:42.880
Kyo!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:48.860
Kawaguchi.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.400
I don't like all this.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.560
I know.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.970
I don't like that attitude, either!

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.970
I know that, too.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:57.960
And you're fine with that?

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.730
You're just fine about leaving things like this?!

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:02.810
No, I'm not.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:04.280
So?

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.270
I don't like this, either!

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:08.040
Good for you!

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:22.430
It's all your fault!

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:23.260
What?!

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:27.560
We never went to the nationals
because of that punch you threw!

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:32.700
It was an unfair call! I couldn't let it go!

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.870
I know that!

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:35.670
What?!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.410
Why couldn't you just
say that from the start?!

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:40.100
Because I don't do excuses!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.750
What, are you some kinda samurai now?!

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:44.980
Shut up! That's just how I am!

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:01.020
Ow...

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:03.760
I'm sorry.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.430
If I'd just accepted the whole thing...

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:10.100
we'd could have gone to the nationals.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.580
I'm sorry.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.210
Dumb ass.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.980
You're not the kind of guy who'd
shut up and take anything.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:23.480
Like a guy who'd just accept that would
win even if he got to the nationals? Idiot...

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:28.620
The truth is... I would've punched
him over a call like that, too.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:30.560
Kawaguchi...

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.390
Wanna go hit him again?

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:35.200
Kidding!

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.770
Ow...

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.370
Damn. I'm bleeding!

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:43.600
Aw, you'll be in the pool soon.
Just leave it.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:45.880
It'll get infected!

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.680
It's chlorinated, remember? Chlorinated.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:52.210
Look, I'm not a damn
savage like you, okay?!

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:04.460
It's Kurage.
What'd he do to make her cry?

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:05.790
No! Look!

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:14.810
Dammit, Kurage!

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.440
What are you doing on
our sacred school grounds?!

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.380
Besides, no fair doing it
in the nurse's office!

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:22.580
Oh, brother...

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:26.150
We were kinda hoping to
keep this quiet for a while.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:30.150
Having you two finding out is like publicly
announcing it to the entire school!

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:33.650
Oh, what's the harm? They'll all just find
out a little sooner than we planned.

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:38.120
Besides...
I have a feeling we should hurry.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.500
Is that not amazing?!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.800
Ol' Kurage actually proposed to Omizu!

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:47.470
Well, I guess I should announce
that I'm going steady with Mizuki.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.670
"Going" steady, huh?

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:52.840
That's great! Everyone's on course
for happiness, full speed ahead!

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.610
And with Kawaguchi joining,
we'll have five members for next term!

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.140
The swim club's survival is in the bag!

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:04.160
Sorry, sorry! Starting tomorrow,
we'll practice seriously, okay?

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.430
Since you guys blew off today's
practice, snacks are on you.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:08.220
What?!
What?!

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:10.430
Okay, while we chow down some okonomiyaki,

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:13.600
we'll come up with a training schedule
that'll take us to the big swim meet.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.620
I wonder if there's still time for us.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:16.800
Uh...

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:18.470
Hold it.

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:21.470
Don't say another thing. Got it?

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:22.710
Sure.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.730
What? What's the secret?
You two finally hit puberty?

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.750
Shut up, you jerk!

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:30.710
Why, you!
Don't call Mizuki a jerk, you... jerk!

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:31.850
What?!

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.880
You and me, right now!

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.420
Guys, please! Don't fight!

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:38.490
<i>It feels like we're back to the old days.</i>

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.720
<i>No... We've moved on.</i>

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:43.560
<i>And once Kaminagi's back, then we can...</i>

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:52.990
Wh... What the?!

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:55.340
What's up, Kyo?

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.480
What's got you looking so weird?

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.280
But... Don't you?!

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.570
I see.

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:02.710
It's too bad.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.700
This is the end, isn't it?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:12.320
Coatlicue is closing in on the Garuda.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.920
We'll attack as soon as we're within
effective firing range. A pincer strike!

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:20.020
Holonic field, forming.
Holonic rifles, both hands!

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:22.300
Entering firing range in five seconds.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.740
Four... Three... Two...

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:25.640
One!

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:26.840
Locked on!

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.770
Fire!

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.640
Did we do it?!

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:45.620
Our light armor's phase shifting!

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:57.030
Increase light armor density!

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:59.670
Route all our Q.L. to support the armor!

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:00.730
Roger!

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:17.790
An attack our light armor can't
protect against... What is it?

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.660
<i>Hraesvelg! We'll cover you!</i>

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:22.190
Negative, Lu-Shen! Stay away from us!

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.330
May-Yu! Holonic Lancer!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:24.950
Okay!

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:46.310
Holonic Launcher!

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.250
What?!

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:20.150
Garuda! Hraesvelg!
Combat level of both is down!

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:21.950
They can't take much more!

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:24.050
It's too dangerous for them
to try and withdraw!

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:25.720
They'll end up like the Altair!

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.350
Soon, they won't have enough
Q.L. to make it back here!

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:30.820
Commander!

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.030
Open gun ports for the G.A.S.P.R.!

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.530
Target the Coatlicue!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:39.770
Transmit the Garuda and Hraesvelg
back here simultaneously as we fire!

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.210
Particle accelerator coil, activated!

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:45.480
Forty...

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:46.610
Eighty...

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:47.130
One hundred!

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:51.150
Main engine, transmission scatter rate, confirmed!

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:53.380
Confirm transition to G.A.S.P.R. mode!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:56.280
Range to enemy target: twelve hundred!

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:59.320
Releasing safety locks!

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:02.680
Particle coil, secondary turbine, open!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.790
Bearing: 8.15! Declination: 0.03!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.900
Particle accelerator coil now at 240!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.440
Enemy target, locked!

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:12.870
FIRE!

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:19.180
Transmit!

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:37.650
Garuda and Hraesvelg have been recovered!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:47.540
Portside armor has been hit!

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.940
Retreat from this area, best speed!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.500
Pellucidar mode, off-line!

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.660
We made it...

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.730
They must have a limit
on their Q.L. charge, too.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:23.310
Our light armor can't protect us from it?

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:25.370
That thing's gonna be a pain to deal with.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:28.670
Kyo is calling!

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:37.580
What the hell is happening?!

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:39.510
The server's failed.

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:44.360
Constantly running this world...

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:47.030
has exceeded the processing
power of the Maihama server.

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:48.200
What?

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.670
There's a limit.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:52.760
It's impossible to simulate
an infinite flow of time.

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.040
That's why it's started to fail.

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:56.970
No way...

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:59.940
Relax. It's not going to break down.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.640
Instead, it's going to reset, soon.

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.850
Except for the data of Cerebrants,

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.790
the people, their memories,
the environment...

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:12.890
Everything here in the world of Maihama
will return to what it was five months ago.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.120
Return?!

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:17.120
Maihama repeats the same time period.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:18.960
Again... and again.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:21.990
So, what happens to us?!

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:24.700
I finally made up with Kawaguchi!

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:29.440
And Kurage's going to marry Omizu!
What about Ushio and Mizuki?!

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:32.440
What happens to the swim club?!
To everyone?!

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.770
This always happens.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.880
You've made up with them
over and over in the past.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.320
Every five months.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:42.310
Can't you stop the reset?!

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:45.220
That's not the problem.

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:48.090
The quantum servers are a
system to preserve people.

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:51.360
All they do is run these programs
we call "people" in order to do that.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.600
But those who are preserved...

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:56.160
are done so within a constantly
repeating realistic dream.

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:58.070
It can't be.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:01.540
It just means that
within the world of data,

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.300
dreams and reality
have the same meaning.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:05.480
Kyo...

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:09.910
You've lived through this summer in
Maihama over a hundred times already.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.750
Kyo...

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:54.350
Maihama is a world
that exists within a time loop.

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:57.550
For us, the first morning of
September will never come.

00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:02.160
Come on, Sogoru. Let's spend the last night
of summer break with everyone, having fun!

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:06.560
Tomorrow, everything we've done or
remember from the past five months will reset.

00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:09.570
You will once more
set out onto the battlefield.

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:12.660
Yeah... The sad battlefield
where Kaminagi awaits you.

00:23:13.340 --> 00:23:16.470
Next time, on Zegapain:
"Battlefield of Rebirth."

00:23:16.470 --> 00:23:18.780
My pain, never to be forgotten.
